        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "e061ceba-0217-5121-a657-b0a349f05b0c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Castle Hill, Monticello, Albemarle County, Virginia, Charlottesville, Southwest Mountains, Paris, France\n- People: Thomas Jefferson, Alfred Landon Rives\n- Topics: Plantations, Historic registers, Engineering\n\nFacts:\n- Thomas Jefferson began designing and building Monticello at age 26 after inheriting the land from his father.\n- Monticello was the primary plantation of Thomas Jefferson, the third President of the United States.\n- Alfred Landon Rives was born on March 25, 1830, in Paris, France.\n- Castle Hill is a historic, privately owned 600-acre plantation at the foot of the Southwest Mountains in Albemarle County, Virginia, near Monticello and Charlottesville.\n- Castle Hill is recognized by the Virginia Landmarks Register and the National Register of Historic Places.\n- Alfred Landon Rives was an American engineer.\n- Alfred Landon Rives died on February 27, 1903, at Castle Hill, Virginia.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
